3. SQL Query for Rating Distribution Pie Chart
The SQL query used for the rating distribution pie chart is:
SELECT
    rating,
    COUNT(*) AS count
FROM performance_reviews
GROUP BY rating;
The performance_reviews table contains multiple review records. Each review has a rating such as:
•	Excellent
•	Good
•	Average
•	Poor
The GROUP BY rating statement groups all records that have the same rating together.
After grouping the records, COUNT(*) counts how many reviews belong to each rating category.
For example, the result may be:
Rating	Count
Excellent	24
Good	30
Average	18
Poor	8
This result is sent from the Flask backend to the React frontend. The RatingPieChart component uses the rating field as the category name and the count field as the size of each pie slice.
Without GROUP BY rating, SQL would return only one total count for all reviews instead of a separate count for each rating category.
