4. What does ResponsiveContainer do in Recharts?
ResponsiveContainer is a component provided by Recharts that automatically adjusts the width and height of a chart based on the size of its parent container.
Example:
<ResponsiveContainer
    width="100%"
    height={300}
>
    <BarChart data={data}>
        ...
    </BarChart>
</ResponsiveContainer>
The width="100%" property means that the chart uses the available width of its parent container.
This is important because the Employee Performance Dashboard may be viewed on different screen sizes such as desktop, tablet, or mobile devices.
Without ResponsiveContainer, a chart may have a fixed width and can overflow, become too small, or not fit correctly when the screen size changes.
By using ResponsiveContainer, the charts automatically resize when their parent container changes size.
Every chart in this project uses ResponsiveContainer so that the KPI analytics dashboard remains responsive and works correctly across different screen sizes.

